Title: Separate raw API outputs from derived artifacts in experiment pipeline
Created: 2026-05-25
Author: HDMX-coding-agent

--- log ---
2026-05-25T06:20Z HDMX-coding-agent created
2026-05-25T12:00Z HDMX-coding-agent superseded — Action 1 (no .md in raw dirs) done via snapshot commits in branch t0291-results-cleanstack-nomd; Action 2 (standalone extractor + exp2_phase_b0_consolidate.py adaptation) tracked in ticket 0292. Close this ticket when the branch merges.

--- body ---
## Context
`exp2_naive_arm.py` writes `{agent}.md` (derived narrative) alongside raw API
outputs during the run itself. This conflates two concerns: data collection and
post-processing. Consequences:
- Improving extraction logic (e.g. table concatenation) requires re-running
  expensive API calls to regenerate `.md`
- Raw output directories are not faithful records of API responses
- `exp2_interactive_smoke.py` already does this correctly (pure raw outputs);
  the naive arm should follow the same discipline

**Must be resolved before committing raw results** so the committed output
directories are clean and re-extractable without re-running the API.

## Relevant files
- `experiments/sota/exp2_naive_arm.py` — writes `{agent}.md` inline (line 393)
- `experiments/sota/exp2_interactive_smoke.py` — reference implementation
  (pure raw outputs, no derived files)
- `experiments/sota/exp2_phase_b0_consolidate.py` — existing consolidation
  script (old flat layout; needs adapting to run{N}/ layout)

## Actions
1. Remove `.md` write from `exp2_naive_arm.py` (line 393-394); keep all raw
   outputs intact
2. Create `experiments/sota/exp2_extract.py` (or extend
   `exp2_phase_b0_consolidate.py`) — a standalone extraction script that:
   - Reads raw outputs for all arms/agents/runs
   - Concatenates sub-tables across turns (fixes 0290 for analysis side)
   - Writes `{agent}.md` per run into a separate `derived/` subdir or alongside
     raw with a clear naming convention
   - Emits updated `summary.json` with correct `inventory_rows`
3. Wire into Makefile as a dependent target after the run target

## Test
After removing `.md` write from naive arm:
```bash
make -f experiment2.mk arm1-run01  # must succeed without writing any .md
ls outputs/sota_exp3_arm1_batch1/run01/*.md  # must be empty (only summary*.md)
```
After adding extract step:
```bash
python sota/exp2_extract.py --arm 1 --run 01
ls outputs/sota_exp3_arm1_batch1/run01/derived/  # should contain {agent}.md
```

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `exp2_naive_arm.py` writes no `.md` files during the run
- [ ] A separate extract script regenerates all `.md` from raw outputs alone
- [ ] Extracted tables concatenate sub-tables (ties into ticket 0290)
- [ ] Existing arm1/arm3 raw results are re-extractable cleanly
- [ ] `make check-fast` passes
